  "hero": "wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Dr-Suzuki-and-Professor-Mark-Radford-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania.jpg",
  "hero_alt": "",
  "excerpt": "Professor Traian Chirila, Professor Mark Radford, and Dr. Shuko Suzuki from QEI working with a team of UMFST researchers, have started on a series of projects that focus on understanding human tissue and their role in novel therapeutic strategies proposed by our scientists for various pathologic conditions.",
  "body_html": "<p>Queensland Eye Institute is excited by our recent collaboration with the George E. Palade University of Medicine, Pharmacy, Science and Technology (UMFST) of Târgu Mureș in Romania.</p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4113\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\" id=\"attachment_4113\" style=\"width: 480px\"><a href=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Dr-Suzuki-and-Robert-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania.jpeg\"><img alt=\"Dr Suzuki and Dr Tripon recording the results provided by the BioTester at UMFST\" class=\"wp-image-4113 size-full\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"640\" sizes=\"(max-width: 480px) 100vw, 480px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Dr-Suzuki-and-Robert-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania.jpeg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Dr-Suzuki-and-Robert-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania.jpeg 480w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Dr-Suzuki-and-Robert-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania-225x300.jpeg 225w\" width=\"480\"/></a><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-4113\">Dr Suzuki and Dr Tripon recording the results provided by the BioTester at UMFST</figcaption></figure>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Professor Traian Chirila, Professor Mark Radford, and Dr. Shuko Suzuki from QEI, working with a team of UMFST researchers (including two PhD students), have started on a series of projects that focus on understanding human tissue and their role in novel therapeutic strategies proposed by our scientists for various pathological conditions.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4108\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\" id=\"attachment_4108\" style=\"width: 640px\"><a href=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Biotester-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania.jpeg\"><img alt=\"BioTester 5000 at (UMFST) in Târgu Mureș Romania\" class=\"wp-image-4108 size-large\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"480\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Biotester-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania-1024x768.jpeg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Biotester-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Biotester-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania-300x225.jpeg 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Biotester-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania-768x576.jpeg 768w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Biotester-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania-1430x1073.jpeg 1430w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Biotester-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania-800x600.jpeg 800w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Biotester-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania-400x300.jpeg 400w\" width=\"640\"/></a><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-4108\">BioTester 5000 at (UMFST) in Târgu Mureș Romania</figcaption></figure>\n<p> </p>\n<p>As part of the agreement, QEI has set up a laboratory, equipped with scientific instrumentation dedicated entirely to these projects. The equipment included the BioTester 5000 (CellScale, Canada), the only tool allowing biaxial evaluation of biological tissues.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-4109\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\" id=\"attachment_4109\" style=\"width: 640px\"><a href=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Dr-Suzuki-and-Professor-Mark-Radford-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania.jpg\"><img alt=\"Dr. Suzuki and Professor Mark Radford preparing the machine for measurements at UMFST\" class=\"wp-image-4109 size-full\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"480\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Dr-Suzuki-and-Professor-Mark-Radford-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania.jpg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Dr-Suzuki-and-Professor-Mark-Radford-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania.jpg 640w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Dr-Suzuki-and-Professor-Mark-Radford-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania-300x225.jpg 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Dr-Suzuki-and-Professor-Mark-Radford-at-George-E.-Palade-University-of-Medicine-Pharmacy-Science-and-Technology-UMFST-of-Târgu-Mures-Romania-400x300.jpg 400w\" width=\"640\"/></a><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-4109\">Dr. Suzuki and Professor Mark Radford preparing the machine for measurements at UMFST</figcaption></figure>\n<p> </p>\n<p>We look forward to bringing you further news about this partnership in upcoming editions.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><em>Chirila, M. Radford, S. Suzuki/5-JULY-2022 </em></p>",
